  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restoring forest connectivity in Uganda&apos;s Albertine Rift for chimpanzee conservation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 1-year project is to enhance the viability of Uganda&apos;s eastern chimpanzee populations by maintaining and restoring connectivity between forests in the northern Albertine Rift. Specific activities include: 1) establishing a robust and effective community-based chimpanzee monitoring program; 2) extend reforestation/afforestation to two critical linkages between forest reserves; and 3) using conservation agriculture, REDD+, environmental education, and small enterprise support to garner greater focus from the Northern Albertine Rift Conservation Group on the target areas.</narrative>
  </description>
